<nigel_wireker. specstult. 767>	Nee tamen invenit quae cupiebat ibi.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 768>	Qualiter Buvnellus deceptus est a mercatore.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 769>	Talia quserentem mercator Londoniensis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 770>	Vidit, et advertens quis fuit ^ inquit ei,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 771>	" Nuncius es raagnus, quisquis te miserit istuc ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 772>	" Maxima namque petis et preciosa nimis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 773>	" Et sapiens et dives erat, quicunque ministrum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 774>	" Hue ita te misit, res manifesta docet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 775>	" Nam facies vultusque tuus satis indieat unde
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 776>	" Veneris, aut quis sis, nee latuisse potes.'*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 777>	" Magnus es, et quaravis peregrini^ tectus amictu,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 778>	" In propria patria non peregrinus eris,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 779>	" O quam sollicita pro te domus est tua tota,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 780>	" Proque tuo reditu vota precesque facit !"
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 781>	\Responsio onercatoris Burnello data.']
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 782>	" Anglia me genuit, Londanis® civibus ortus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 783>	" Prsesulis hue veni nuncius ipse mei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 784>	" Cui quia plus sequo nasum natura retraxit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 785>	" Institit arte malum posse levare suum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 786>	" Quatuor ergo viros partes transmisit ad istas.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 787>	" Prgesul, ob banc eausam conditione gravem
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 788>	" Annus et annus abit ex quo pervenimus istae,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 789>	" Tresque vise comites mors tulit una meos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 790>	" Hie teneo species '^ quas, si fortuna dedisset
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 791>	" Posse referre domum maxima cura foret.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 792>	" Quicquid in bac urbe venisti quaerere, totum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 793>	" Signatum teneo depositumque domi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 794>	" Sumptibus assumptis, alieni debitor feris
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 795>	" Aretor, et in patriam non licet ire meam,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 796>	" Uror amore tamen patriae, tantoque reverti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 797>	" Anxius exopto quo magis ire vetor.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 798>	" Litera certa mibi patris de funere venit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 799>	" Fama sed et dominum fingit obisse * meum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 800>	" Vitrea vasa decern milii sunt, et cuncta repleta'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 801>	" His aliisque simul quae tua charta** notat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 802>	" Si precium dederis quo res mihi constitit ipsa,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 803>	" Cras potes in patriam dives abire tuam.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 804>	" Ulterius precio ' peregrinus de peregrino
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 805>	" Absit ut accipiam, rem tibi dando meam.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 806>	" Hoc tamen excepto,^ quia te puto religiosum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 807>	" Ut liceat precibus participare tuis."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 808>	IHio fit contractus inter BurnelluTn et mercatoreTn.]
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 809>	Illico Burnellus precium numeravit,^ et ilia
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 810>	Nugis vasa decem plena recepit ibi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 811>	Quoque magis fieret stabilis contractus, utrimque^*^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 812>	Nomen vendentis ^^ poscit, et ille refert.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 813>	" Londoniis natus Gila ^'^ de matre, parentis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 814>	" Nomine Truffator nuncupor ipse mei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 815>	" Bula ^ mihi soror est, multis notissima regnis ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 816>	" Est et Truifa ^ mihi foedere juncta toro.'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 817>	" Nee minus ipse tuum nomen mihi dicere dignum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 818>	" Duxeris, ut memori mente tenere queam."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 819>	Inanis jactantia Burnelli [de sua nobilitate].^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 820>	" Nomen Burnellus mihi stat," respondit^ asellus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 821>	" Notus ubique satis nomine reque simul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 822>	" Principibus regni necnon et regibus ipsis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 823>	" Servio, servili conditione carens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 824>	" Et pater et proavus regum de more ministri
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 825>	" Semper erant et erunt tempus in omne suum.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 826>	" Regis in obsequium successi jure paterno,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 827>	" Indiget officio curia tota meo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 828>	" Obvius ipse mihi si rex quandoque feratur,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 829>	" Cedit, et incedo rege ferente locum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 830>	" Est tamen una mihi multum contraria pestis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 831>	" Rusticus immitis, exitiale malum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 832>	" Semper enim stimulos gerit, aut nodosa flagella,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 833>	" Aut graditur canibus cinctus utrumque latus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 834>	" Huic pater exosus meus extitit, atque parentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 835>	" Deque meo genere quicquid in orbe fuit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 836>	" Principis et procerum mores satis approbo, quorum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 837>	" Risus, verba, jocus, dulcis arnica, decentj
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 838>	" Rex mihi dicit, Ave ! per eum dum transeo ; vse vse !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 839>	" Fructifer ingeminat rusticus, orbis onus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 840>	" Impetat hunc scabies, hunc cotidiana perurat,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 841>	" Ne possit vel eques ipse vel ire pedes.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 842>	found only in P. altered /jer!<ra< to perurant, to make
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 843>	" Faucibus insideat mala gutta, caputque fatigot,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 844>	" Defluat et venter nocte dieque suus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 845>	" Durus ei dominus longum succedat in tyvum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 846>	" Rixentur semper uxor et ipse simul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 847>	" Hunc pedis a planta summotenus ore perurant
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 848>	" Ulcera, quae seateant vermibus atque lue.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 849>	" Hunc ego commendo Sathanse, de stercore cujus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 850>	" Dicitur esse satus, quod probat ipse satis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 851>	" Hunc ego si possem totum delere per orbem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 852>	" Nullus ei fieret urbe vel orbe locus."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 853>	Qualiter Burnellus rediit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 854>	His igitur ^ dictis, patrias Burnellus ad oras
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 855>	Lpetus et exultans mane redire parat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 856>	Crastina lux aderat, Burnellus onustus ab urbe
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 857>	Exit, et exsolvit vota precesque Deo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 858>	Casibus in Isetis quam sit vicina ruina,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 859>	Et lapsus facilis nemo videre potest
