<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1100>	Froniundum Rodani fecit ad iraa velii.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1101>	Interceptus aquis mortem gustavit in undis ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1102>	Lusvis et est propriis artibus ipse prior.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1103>	Tunc cecinit carmen resonum Burnellus, et altis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1104>	Vocibus exultans, ora resolvit ita.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1105>	Caniiciim Burnelll [2)ost proiciintationem Fwmundi.]
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1106>	" Cantemus, socii ! festum celebremus, aselli !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1107>	" Vocibus et votis organa nostra sonent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1108>	" Exultent asini, l?eti modulentur aselli,*'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1109>	" Laude sonent celebri tympana, sistra,' chori !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1110>	" Grimbaldus periit, sociique sui perierunt;^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1111>	" Mors liostes rapuit quatuor una meos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1112>	" Fromundus cecidit, Rodani submer-sus in undis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1113>	" Lusus et est subito legibus ipse suis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1114>	" Incidit in laqueos frater Fromundus iniquos,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1115>	" Quos tamen ipse sibi texuit arte sua.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1116>	" Quern voluit sapiens stultura delere scienter,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1117>	" Stultus et ignorans prsecipitavit eum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1118>	" Corruit in foveam prseceps Fromundus, in illam
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1119>	" Quern manibus propriis. foderat ipse prius.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1120>	" Ne via longa foret, saltu Fromundus in uno
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1121>	" Complevit cursum nescius ipse suum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1122>	" Saltus erat subitus, rupes prserupta deorsum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1123>	" Fluminis unda rapax, alveus absque vadis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1124>	" Quern ^ nunquam didicit saltum ^ docuisse probatur
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1125>	" Non opus est alio, suflScit unus ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1126>	" Exultefc Eodanus celebri de laude triumphi !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1127>	" Fromundus cecidit, florida psallat humus I
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1128>	[Sepultura fratris Fromundi.']
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1129>	Mortuus est igitur^ postquam Fromundus, et undis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1130>	Extraetus, patrio sunt data membra solo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1131>	Cujus busta videns cum pertransiret asellus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1132>	Flevit, et inciso marmore scripsit ita.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1133>	Epitaphium fratris Fromundi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1134>	" Fratribus exemplum frater Fromundus in pevum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1135>	" Hunc titulum vivo cepit ab hoste suo
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1136>	" Quem celer ac sapiens stultum tardumque putavit*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1137>	" Fallere, prpeveniens ipse fefellit eum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1138>	" Sic tardus celerem, sic sic stultus sapientem
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1139>	" In saltu celeri desipuisse dedit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1140>	" Sic fraus fraude perit, sic ars deluditur arte,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1141>	" Sic dolus et fraudes proemia digna ferunt.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1142>	" Saltus Fromundi fratres memorentur ^ iniqui,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1143>	" Prosit, ut a simili nota figura mali."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1144>	[Bwnellus caucla amissa de statu auo fufuro prcecogitat]
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1145>	His igitur^ gestis patrias Burnellus ad oras
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1146>	Festinat celeri corpore, mente, pede.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1147>	Sed quia pauper erat, expensa deficiente,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1148>	Mendicando suum ssepe retardat iter.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1149>	Ssepe suos casus secum memorando retractat,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1150>	Dixerat et dudum quid Galienus ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1151>	Quoque magis pensat proprise '^ discrimina sortis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1152>	Se magis accusat,^ sic sibi ssepe loquens
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1153>	[Locutio Burnelli seipsurti redarguendo de inertia et stultitia.]
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1154>	" Non sum Burnellus sapiens, sed iners, et asellus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1155>	" Semper, et in primis stultus, hebesque nimis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1156>	" Stultus ego natus sum, stultus et ante creatus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1157>	" Quamque diu fuero, non nisi stultus ero.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1158>	" Stultus et ipse pater meus, et stultissima mater,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1159>	" Dat natui-a milii desipuisse mea.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1160>	" Quod natura dedit, quod tractu temporis hgesit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1161>	" Hseret, et est remanens, nee removetur idem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1162>	" Vah ! quis ego? quid ego?* qualis? quantum que pudendus?^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1163>	" Si bene perpendam, nescio, quid sit ego?^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1164>	" En ego consumpsi pariter cum corpore sumptus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1165>	" Cumque labore meo tempus et ipse meum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1166>	" Jamque satis senui, nee adhuc nisi desipuisse
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1167>	" Me fateor facto, res facit ipsa fidem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1168>	" In sene sensus hebes multum solet esse pudori
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1169>	" Ni sensus sapiant,^ est pudor esse senem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1170>	" Vertitur in risus juvenum delira senectus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1171>	" Nee redimunt * damnum tempora lapsa suum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1172>	" Quantumcunque senex sapiat, tamen ecce juventus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1173>	" Semper delirum somniat esse senem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1174>	" Et si deliret ^ quisquam, pariterque senescat,''
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1175>	" Judicio juvenum nil nisi stultus erit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1176>	" Hoc habet innatum multis comitata senectus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1177>	" Quo plus desipiat plus sapuisse putet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1178>	" Nosse satis potui verbis vultuque magistri,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1179>	" Quam** mea vota forent a ratione procul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1180>	" Ha ! quotiens voluit ea quae nocitura putabat
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1181>	" Dissuadere mihi, si licuisset ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1182>	" Sed furor infelix et mens mea coeca futuri
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1183>	" Sprevit, et irrisit utile quodque magis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1184>	" Et quid erit propriam cum mane revertar in urbem,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1185>	" Non demutata ^ conditione mea ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1186>	" Error posterior pejor quandoque priore
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1187>	" Esse solet ; vereor posteriora mea.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1188>	" Nonne revertentem prseses populusque videbunt ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1189>	" Nonne meos casus curia tota sciet ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1190>	" Diceturque mihi, ' Qualis dicessit ab urbe,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1191>	" ' Ecce reversus adest, nil novitatis habens !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1192>	" Ista quidem dici possent, si, quae modo non est,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1193>	" Integi'a cauda foret ut fuit ante mihi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1194>	*' Ergo quid inspecto tanto discrimine dicent ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1195>	" Num poterunt risus continuisse suos?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1196>	** Risus ero populis, risus totius et urbis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1197>	" Risus erit magno cauda recisa foro.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1198>	" Si non ante fuit populi Burnellus in ore,
