<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1228>	thus :— onus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1229>	" Parisius veniam, studioqiie vacando decenui
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1230>	" Artibus insistam ; non remorabor iter.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1231>	" Postea Boloniam ^ Domino ducente revertar,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1232>	" Legales apices conciliare milii.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1233>	" Paofina divina necnon decreta labonira
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1234>	" Finis erunt, fuerit si mihi vita comes.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1235>	" Sicque meum ^ nomen alio prseeunte Magister
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1236>	" Burnellus dicai' nomine reque siraul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1237>	" Si quis Burnellum non addens forte Magistrum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1238>	" Dixerit, ille milii publiciis liostis erit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1239>	" Norainis ergo mei fama piteeunte celebri,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1240>	" Subsequar orator publicus, absque pari.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1241>	" Obvius adveniet populo comitante senatus;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1242>	" Plebs ruet et dicet, ' Ecce Magister adest !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1243>	" Pnesnlis et fratrum concors sententia, nostro
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1244>	" Se volet auxilio consilioque regi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1245>	" Illud erit stabile quod nos statuemus in urbe,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1246>	" Verba sed et nostra^ legis ad instar erunt,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1247>	" Quod minus in cauda, quod et sequo majus in aure,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1248>	" Tunc fnerit, redimet nomen honore suo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1249>	" Majus erit lucrum nostrum quam damna fuerunt
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1250>	" Gloria finalis crimina cuncta teget." "*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1251>	Qualiter Burnellus vadit Parisius, et de ejus comite in via.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1252>	Talia dum replicat, comes est sociatus eunti,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1253>	Parisius tendens sarcinulasque ferens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1254>	Cui Burnellus ait, dicto dedit oscula, quaerens
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1255>	Quis sit, et unde satus,^ quo citus ire velit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1256>	Ille refert, " Siculus ego sum, cupiensque doceri
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1257>	" Parisius propero ; sit via tuta, precor !"
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1258>	Qualiter Brunellus vadens Parisios
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1259>	"^ Sitque meum, P, invenit in via socium Gerhardum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1260>	Cui Burnellus ait, " Tria sunt communia nobis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1261>	" Votum, causa, solum ; sit via quarta, peto."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1262>	Annuit Arnoldus,' socioque ferenda petenti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1263>	Capsas et libros tradidifc ille suos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1264>	Inde simul dextris sociali foedere junctis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1265>	Pai'isius properant pectore, voce, pede.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1266>	Dumque ^ simul pergunt, socio Burnellus eunti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1267>	Quis sit et unde refert, quae sibi causa vise,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1268>	Quos tulerit casus, quse sit discrimina passus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1269>	Qualiter acciderint ilia vel ilia sibi
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1270>	Qualiter a patria primo discessit, et ad quid,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1271>	Consilium dederat quod Galienus ei ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1272>	Brunettse casus varios, causamque ^ Bicornis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1273>	Actibus expositis tempus utrumque notans
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1274>	Qualiter accepit a Truffatore Salerni,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1275>	Londoniis orto,^ vitrea vasa decem ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1276>	Qua ratione canes frater Fromundus in ilium
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1277>	Miserit, et quantum perdidit ipse miser ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1278>	Inde canum mortem narrat, saltumque sequentem
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1279>	Fratris Fromundi, judiciumque Dei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1280>	Addidit et titulos bustali marmore scriptos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1281>	Nunc quoque Parisius qua ratione petat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1282>	Talia dicenti casusque suos memoranti,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1283>	Keddidit Arnoldus ^ talia dicta ^ sibi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1284>	Narratio Arnoldi de filio preshyteri et pullo gallince.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1285>	" Quam variis vicibus humanse res variantur,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1286>	" Non est res facilis dinumerasse '^ milii.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1287>	" Quam minima causa magnum discrimen oriri
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1288>	" Possit, ab effectu res manifesta docet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1289>	" Contigit Apulise, celebri res digna relatu,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1290>	" Tempore Willelmi principis hujus avi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1291>	" Presbyter urbanus quidam, digressus ab urbc
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1292>	" Longius, agrestem coepit habere casam.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1293>	" Cui bene^ temporibiis cunctis sua rura colenti,'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1294>	" Multotiens segetum copia multa fuit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1295>	" Fecerat et natos propria de conjuge, dici
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1296>	" Conjux presbyteri si licet absque nota.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1297>	'' Quorum Gundulfum quendam, quern vidimus ipsi,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1298>	" Cum puer esset adhuc, contigit esse domi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1299>	" Cumque foret fiugum custos patris, ostia servans,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1300>	" Consuevit virgam ssepe tenere manu.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1301>	" Accidit ^ ergo semel, pullis comitantibus ejus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1302>	" Coppa quod intraret horrea/ grana legens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1303>	" Cumque suam matrem pulli sequerentur egentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1304>	" Ostia presserunt improbitate sua
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1305>	" Quos puer elata virga quam forte tenebat
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1306>	" Csedere praesumpsit atque fugare foras.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1307>	" Qui, quoniam turbatus erat, plus institit fequo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1308>	" Transgressus verbis verberibusque modum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1309>	" Ira quid expediat, dum non discernit, inique
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1310>	" Plurima dispensat praecipitando gradum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1311>	" Ssepe levi jactu constat jactura perennis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1312>	" Atque levi puncto pignora cara cadunt.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1313>	" Cumque puer virgam nimis exerceret in iram,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1314>	" Contigit ut pulli tibia fracta foret.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1315>	" Tibia fracta diu puUo pariterque parenti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1316>	" Tristitise causa non mediocris erat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1317>	" Hinc dolor, hincque pudor, pullum stimulavit in " iram,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1318>	" Ut cuperet puero redd ere posse vicem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1319>	" Tempore crescente caro consolidata recrevit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1320>	" Obduxitque cutis vulnera veste nova.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1321>	" Ossa diu fracta multum^ doluere dolore,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1322>	" Vulneris inflicti corde tenente notam.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1323>	" V alliens exterius satis est obducta cicatrix ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1324>	" Cruda sed interius vulnera corda tenent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1325>	" Jam proscripta diu, proprias remeavit ad oras
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1326>	" Tibia, sed ftxcti mens meraor exul agit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1327>	" Pes graditur recte, femur est sine vulnere sanum ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1328>	" Nil sapit elisum, tibia sana coit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1329>	" Claudicat ast animus, pectus sine vulnere languct,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1330>	" Cor queritur, mens est ulcere plena gravi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1331>	" Ultio suspensa, sine qua mens liBsa quieti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1332>	" Nil habet, expectat pervigil ante fores.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1333>	" Nulla quies mentis Isesse, nullumque levamen,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1334>	" Nil nisi vindicta pectora Isesa levat.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1335>	" Non mergus stagnum, fugientem non lupus agnum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1336>	, " Turba canum leporem, vel fera capta fugam ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1337>	" Nee plus piscis aquam, nee ave plus nisus alaudam,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1338>	" Quam mens vindictam Isesa videre cupit.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1339>	" Sic quoque Gundulfi pullus cupiebat iniqui
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1340>	" Sumere vindictam, si locus esset ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1341>	" Creverat in gallum sextum jam pullus in annum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1342>	" Fungens ^ defuncti patris honore sui.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1343>	" Creverat et multum* jam jam Gundulfus in altum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1344>	" Jamque suo patri substituendus erat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1345>	" Jam nihil obstabat, jam nil deerat, nisi solus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1346>	" Ordo sacerdotis nuper habendus ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1347>	" Prsesul enim victus precibus meritisque beati
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1348>	" Rufini vota censuit esse rata,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1349>	" Constituitque diem quo sanctiticatio tanta
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1350>	" Debuit impend! more, modoque ^ loci.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1351>	" Sabbata Natalem Domini praeeuntia festum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1352>	" Terminus est positus,*" urbs Tarabella ^ locus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1353>	" Gundulfum provehi cupiunt gaudentque parentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1354>	" Jamque parant festis munera digna suis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1355>	" Ante diem festum generalia festa parentes'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1356>	" Ut fficiant, veniunfc eonveniuntque simul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1357>	" Aula patet cunctis, onerant cibaria mensas,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1358>	" Indulgentque nimis potibus atque cibis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1359>	" Bacchus adest festo, patulo diffusus in auro,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1360>	" Exhilarans populum sanctificansque locum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1361>	" Nox aderat, qua ^ mane citus Gundulfus ad urbem *
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1362>	" Profecturus erat, sanctificandus ibi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1363>	" Ad gallicantus primes iter arripiendum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1364>	" Esse volunt, aberat nam locus ille procul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1365>	" Mandatur famulis tempus, prsescribitur bora,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1366>	" Qua profecturus mane citandus erit ; ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1367>	" Scilicet ut studeant cantus audire priores
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1368>	" Quos dederit gallus nuncius ante diem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1369>	" Sufficietque^ satis si tunc surrexerit ille,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1370>	" Nam nox longa nimis, nee grave restat iter.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1371>	" Gallus ut bcec verba vigili percepit in aure,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1372>	" Gaudet, et exultat pectore, voce tacens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1373>	" Tanta quidem super his fuit exultatio cordis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1374>	" Ora quod a laude vix cohibere potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1375>	" Quodque prseoptabat multum differre tacendo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1376>	" Vocibus explosis accelerare parat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1377>	" Quam dolor excludit immutant^ gaudia vocem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1378>	" Hsec sua plectra monent, hie reticei'e jubet.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1379>	" Inter utrumque manens, neutri consentit, utroque
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1380>	" Vincitur, et vincit, voce tacente tamen.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1381>	" Jam nox tota fere fuerat consumpta bibendo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1382>	" Cum jam fessa mero dant sua membra toro.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1383>	" Tempera nocturna, studio delusa bibentum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1384>	" Nee bene distincta, prseteriere cito.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1385>	" Nee mora potantum potuit noctem remorari,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1386>	" Quin non consueta lege ligaret eos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1387>	" Affuit interea cantandi temporis hora,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1388>	" Sed cantor vocem supprimit^ atque sonum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1389>	" Vox silet, et cantor, potus^ siluere ministri,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1390>	" Pocula, nox, somnus quos vigilare vetant.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1391>	" Admiransque diu gallina silentia gaUi,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1392>	" Et quod ab officio cederet ipse suo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1393>	" Leviter accedens sponso, suggessit in aure,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1394>	" Quod jam transissent tempus et hora simul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1395>	" Qui respondit ita, ' Noli vexare, quiesce !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1396>	" ' Semper eris stulta ; stulta, recede, precor
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1397>	" ' Vse cui stulta comes sociali foedere nupsit
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1398>	" * Non erit illius absque dolore torus/
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1399>	" Nee minus ilia tamen, nimis importuna, marito
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1400>	" Institit, ut noctis tempora certa notet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1401>	" Ille sed e contra tentans cohibere loquacem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1402>	" Porrigit inde preces, intonat inde minas.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1403>	" Ilia tamen jurat, nisi tanta silentia solvat
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1404>	" Ille, quod ilia canet, concutietque domum;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1405>	" Impatiensque morse, raucas de gutture voces
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1406>	" Profert, quaque potest voce sonare sonat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1407>	" Qua tamen audita, quidam respondit eidem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1408>	" ' Desine, Coppa, precor, nam nihil est quod agis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1409>	" ' Quamvis gallina nocturno temi^ore cantet,*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1410>	" ' Non ideo citius lux oriimda venit.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1411>	" Nox^ ruit interea, domus ebrietate profunda
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1412>	" Tota sepulta jacet, dormit et ijise vigil.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1413>	" Omnia somnus iners operit, Gundulfus et ipse
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1414>	" Dormit, et in somnis somnia grata videt.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1415>	Somnium OuTidulfi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1416>	" Ordine suscepto jam se putat esse reversum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1417>	" Indutusque sacris jam celebrare parat.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1418>	" Cantorisque videt niveo sub tegmine gallum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1419>	" Obtiniiisse vices, atque tenere chorum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1420>	" Introitus missse, quem gallus voce sonora
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1421>	" Omnibus invitis intulit, iste fuit
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1422>	" ' Omnia quae, domine,^ nobis fecisse videris,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1423>	" ' Judicio justo facta fuisse liquet.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1424>	" Cumque ^ calix magnus vinoque repletus, adesset,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1425>	" Hausit, et a fundo viscera tota tulit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1426>	" Cumque calix saperet, absumptus et ipse fuisset,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1427>	" Csetera perfecit ordine cuncta suo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1428>	" Sed finem missee, cum cantor debuit, ' Ite/
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1429>	" Dicere, conticuit, signa nee ulla dedit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1430>	" Talibus obstupuit visis Gundulfus, et altis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1431>	" Vocibus exclamans,* ' Est,' ait, ' estne dies ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1432>	" Cui respondentes famuli dixere, volenti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1433>	" Surgere, ' Sustineas, tempus adesse tuum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1434>	" ' Nondum cantavit gallus, qui tempora noctis ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1435>	" ' Novit et assignat singula voce sua.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1436>	" ' Quamvis vellemus furari tempora, nobis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1437>	" ' Invitis, gallus significaret ea.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1438>	" ' Novit enim melius quam nos discrimina noctis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1439>	" ' Pars quota transierit, pars quota restat adhuc.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1440>	" ' Commitamus ei surgentes tempora noctis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1441>	" ' Qui non dormitat sit vigil ille tuus.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1442>	" ' Nox est longa nimis, superest pars maxima ' nobis ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1443>	" ' Verte latus, dormi, non breve tempus habes.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1444>	" ' Nox hiemalis enim tribus est peiionga diebus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1445>	" * Nee sub ' momento dissiluisse potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1446>	" ' Nos vigiles eriraus, gallo mediante fideli,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1447>	" ' Qui quamvis vellet subticuisse nequit/
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1448>	" Gallus ad hfec tacite gallinre dixit in aure,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1449>	" ' Obses ego vobis nee fidejussor ero.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1450>	*• ' Ut poterit,^ fiat, lex est, quam tessera ^ dictat
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1451>	" ' Qui jacet, hie jaceat, qui bibit, ille bibat.' ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1452>	" Dum loqueretur ita, clarum jam mane fenestras
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1453>	" Intrat, et ad rimas lux manifesta ruit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1454>	" Jam Phoebus radios toto difFuderat orbe,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1455>	" Jamque bobus junctis vergit arator humum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1456>	" Gundulfus surgens, et palmis pectora tmidens,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1457>	" * En/ ait, ' en mallem mortuus esse modo !
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1458>	" Et nimis accelerans, strato femoralia linquens,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1459>	" Protinus ad stabulum sternere currit equum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1460>	" Frenum cum sella transacta nocte bubulci
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1461>	" Transtulerant, solito nee fuit ilia loco.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1462>	" Insilit ille*' tamen, frenum redimente capistro,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1463>	" Nee redit ^ ad patrem qui ^ benedicat ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1464>	" Fortiter elisus ^ cursu dum transvolat urbem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1465>	" Corruit in terram, largus '^^ aberrat equus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1466>	" Institit ergo pedes, sed cum pervenit in nrbem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1467>	" Ordinibus factis, serior hora fuit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1468>	" Omnibus expletis pr?esul secesserat aris,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1469>	" Nee locus exstabat, nee fuit hora super.^^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1470>	" Lectio tota fuit perlecta, legensque ' Tu autem,'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1471>	" Dixerat, et pueri vox resonarat ' Amen.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1472>	" Quid faceret Gundulfus ad hsec,^^ medicina dolori
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1473>	" Restabat nulla quam^^ remeare domum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1474>	" Ergo domum propere tristis, multumque^ pudove
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1475>	" Confusus, rediit,^ flensque gemensque satis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1476>	" Hinc pater, inde parens, cum tota prole parentum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1477>	" Gimdulfum plangunt pectore, voce, manu.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1478>	" Confusi redeunt qui convenere parentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1479>	" In lacrimas etenim gaudia versa vident.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1480>	" Arguit liic vigiles, causatur et ille bibentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1481>	" Impetit hie gallum, damnat et ille merura.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1482>	" Talibus auditis, nido gallina relicto
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1483>	" Exiit, et gallo talia verba refert.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1484>	Querimonia gallince.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1485>	" ' Gundulfus noster rediit frustratus ab urbe,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1486>	" ' Tristis, et in lacrimas totus abire parat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1487>	" ' Et pater, et genetrix, fratres,^ miserseque sorores
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1488>	" ' In lacrimas abeunt ; omnia * luctus habent.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1489>	" ' Quamvis Gundulfus laqueo suspensus obisset,*'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1490>	" ' Non possent ejus funera flere magis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1491>	" ' Imponuntque tibi culpam discriminis hujus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1492>	" ' Sis quasi totius causa caputque mali.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1493>	Sententia galli.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1494>	" Talia dicenti gallus respondit, ' Iniquam
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1495>	" 'Non puto, sed dignam, pro vice dare^ vicem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1496>	" ' Pullus eram quondam, Gundulfo percutiente,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1497>	" ' Tibia fracta fuit, ipse recordor adhuc.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1498>	" ' Materiam prior ipse milii causamque doloris
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1499>	" ' Intulit, indicio tibia fracta manet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1500>	" ' Ipse prior risit, dum vulnera nostra dolercnt,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1501>	" ' Nunc ego derisum rideo lege pari.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1502>	" ' Sic variat fortuna vices, sic gaudia luctus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1503>	" ' Occupat, excelsa sic cecidisse solent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1504>	Exoptata diu dulcis medicina dolorum/
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1505>	' * Sero licet veniat, grata venire solet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1506>	Nunquam sera ^ venit morbi medicina cruenti,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1507>	' ' Quolibet antidoto dummodo curet eum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1508>	QujB venit ex facili, nullo prseeunte labore,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1509>	' Ultio delicti, dulcior ilia venit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1510>	Lsetus ab hoste meo victor sine csede * triumpho,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1511>	• ' Ultus et est animus ore tacente meo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1512>	Bella gerant^ alii, sint nostra silentia nobis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1513>	' Voce tubisque tonent,^ nos tacuisse juvat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1514>	Quo levius nobis cessit victoria belli,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1515>	' Victoris tanto gloria major erit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1516>	Non opus est armis, ubi vox suppressa triumphat ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1517>	' Qui bene dissimulat et tacet, ille sapit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1518>	Hostibus ergo meis lacrimse pro sanguine stillent,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1519>	' Vulneris obtineant ira dolorque vicem.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1520>	Vulnus enim cordis dolor est, graviusque perurit
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1521>	' Intima quam giadius exteriora secat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1522>	Exterioris enim levis est medicina doloris,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1523>	' Sed vix aut nunquam saucia corda vigent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1524>	Serius adraittit animus solatia Icesus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1525>	' Quam medicinales saucia membra manus.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1526>	Vix ea fatus erat gallus, cum morte soluti
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1527>	Cesserunt pariter bine pater, inde parens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1528>	Mox, patre defuncto, patris est Gundulfus ab sede
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1529>	Pulsus, et exterius tradita tota domus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1530>	Gundulfusque miser, pauper, mendicus, et omni
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1531>	Auxilio vacuus, cessit ab urbe procul.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1532>	Mansit apud multos tamen hoc memorabile factum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1533>	Hocque patres natis ssepe referre solent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1534>	Ut memores facti sic se moderentur ubique,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1535>	Ne de post facto ^ poenituisse queant."
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1536>	Qualiter Burnellus venit Parisius, et quid fecerit ibi}
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1537>	Talia cum ^ pariter gradientes plura referrent,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1538>	Parisius veniunt,^ hospitiumque petunt.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1539>	Corpora fessa quies recreat, tenuisqus difetse
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1540>	Damna recompensat * rnensa calixque frequens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1541>	Ossa, cutem, nervos, quge vel labor aut via longa
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1542>	Quassarat, refovent balnea, cura, quies.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1543>	Burnellusque sibi minuit erinesque totondit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1544>	Induit et tunica se meliore sua,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1545>	Pexus et ablutus, tandem progressus in urbera
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1546>	Intrat in ecclesiam, vota precesque facit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1547>	Inde scholas adiens, secum deliberat utrum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1548>	Expediant potius ista vel ilia sibi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1549>	Et quia subtiles sensu considerat Anglos,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1550>	Pluribus ex causis se sociavit eis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1551>	Moribus egregii, verbo vultuque venusti,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1552>	Ingenio pollent, consilioque vigent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1553>	Dona pluunt populis, et detestantuv avaris,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1554>	Fercula multiplicant, et sine lege bibunt.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1555>	Wessail et dringail,*' necnon persona secunda,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1556>	Ha3C tria sunt vitia quae comitantur eos.''
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1557>	His tribus exceptis, nihil est quod in his reprehendas
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1558>	Haec tria si tollas, C£etera cuncta placent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1559>	Nee tamen hsec ita^ sunt semper reprobanda, quod iUis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1560>	Esse locus nequeat tempore sive loco.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1561>	Nam duo prsecipue sunt exclusiva dolorum,''
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1562>	Ltetitieeque vias insinuare solent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1563>	Brunelhs venit Parisios cum Ger- ^ Wesseyl cum drincheyl, B,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1564>	Tertia res cohibet, quo ' dicitur esse referta
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1565>	Gallia fermentura ne ^ nocuisse queat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1566>	Hinc comes Angligenis^ prudens desiderat esse,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1567>	Possit ut illorum eonditione frui.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1568>	Est in eis etiam quiddam, nam publica ^ fama
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1569>	Somniat adjungi cur magis optet eos.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1570>	Si de convictu mores formantur eisdem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1571>	Cur nihil accrescat si comes esse queat ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1572>	Si quid eis prseter sortem natura ministrat,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1573>	Ante retrove^ bonum cur nihil inde ferat?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1574>	Accelerans igitur studio, studiosis ^ adhsesit,"
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1575>	Ut discat lepide grammaticeque loqui.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1576>	Sed quia sensus hebes, cervix prpedura, magistri
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1577>	Dogmata non recipit, cura laborque perit.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1578>	Jam pertransierat Burnellus tempora multa,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1579>	Et prope completus septimus annus erat.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1580>	Cum nihil ex toto quodcunque, docente magistro
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1581>	Aut socio, potuit discere '^ prjeter ya.*^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1582>	Quod natura dedit, quod secum detulit illuc,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1583>	Hoc habet, hoc illo nemo tulisse potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1584>	Cura magistrorum multumque diu laborabat,^"
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1585>	Demum defecit, victa labore gravi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1586>	Dorso se baculus, lateri se virga frequenter
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1587>	Applicat, et ferulam sustinuere manus.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1588>	Semper ya^ repetit, nihil est quod dicere possit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1589>	Affectus quovis verbere, prseter ya.^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1590>	Vellicat hie aurem, nasum quatit ille recurvum,^^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1591>	Excutit hie dentes, perforat ille cutem.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1592>	Hie secat, hie urit, hinc solvitur, inde ligatur,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1593>	Intonat iste minas, porrigit ille preces.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1594>	Sic in eo certant ars et natura vicissim,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1595>	Ars rogat, ilia jubefc, litec abit, ilia manet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1596>	Quorum principia constant vitiosa fuisse,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1597>	Aut vix aut nunquam convaluisse valent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1598>	A puero didicit Burnellus ya;^ nihil- ultra
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1599>	Quam quod natura dat retinere potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1600>	Quod fuit innatum servat natura, quod artis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1601>	Sic abit, ut vento pulvis abire solet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1602>	Pevdidit expensas, periitque labor, sed et omne^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1603>	Quod fuit impensum conditione pari.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1604>	Spes quoque deperiit caudiB superinstituendre,"*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1605>	Sentit^ et Anglorum carmina*^ falsa fore.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1606>	Confessio'' BiirnelU lyrce angustia, [et quomodo repreheudit se, cwni riihil profecit]}
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1607>	Ergo recordatus tandem Burnellus ineptfe ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1608>	Daraua juventutis, se reprehendit ita:
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1609>	" Heu mihi ! quod vixi,^*^ quis me furor egit, ut istas
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1610>	" Aggrederer partes Parisiique scliolas ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1611>	" Quid mihi cum studio, cunctoque labore petito ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1612>	" Nonne satis potuit esse Cremona '^ mihi ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1613>	" Alpibus emensis^'^ et post mea terga relictis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1614>	" Stultus in extremis partibus orbis^^ agor.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1615>	" Ut quid " in has partes patriaque domoque relictis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1616>	" Trans Rodanum veni, regna videre nova ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1617>	" Quae mihi cura fuit per tanta pericula mortis
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1618>	" Cernere Francigenas Parisiique scholas
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1619>	" Nosse vel Angligenas^^ largos, Gallosque "^ teuaces,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1620>	" Hos calices, illos multiplicare minas.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1621>	" Appnlus hue veni, sed Gallicus ecce reverter ; ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1622>	" Burnellusque tamen qui fuit ante maiiet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1623>	" Hie nihil addidici, modicumque quod ante""^ scieLam
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1624>	" Hie eofo me totum dedidicisse scio.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1625>	" Galliea verba duo tantum retinere loquique
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1626>	" Si possem, certe gratia magna foret.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1627>	" Quod si forte tria, vel multum quatuor,^ essem
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1628>	" Par Jovis, aut major crederer esse Jove
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1629>	" Italiam facerem tanto trepidare timore,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1630>	" Quod mihi rex ipse certa tributa daret.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1631>	" Tune ego Parisius in vanura non adivissem,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1632>	" Si subjecta foret sic mea"* terra mihi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1633>	" Non modo vadit ita ; longo ° mea stamina Parcse ^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1634>	" Veneruut^ aliter quam mea vota forent.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1635>	" Dura mihi certe multum, sed fata^ fuerunt,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1636>	" Qua) mala multa mihi nilque dedere boni.'-^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1637>	" Quod satis apparet, quia toto pejor in orbe
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1638>	" Non est conditio conditione mea.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1639>	" Sensus hebes mens est et saxo ^** durior omni,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1640>	" Durius hoe pectus est adamante meum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1641>	" Coi", caput, et cerebrum sunt ponderis atqui metalli
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1642>	" Ejusdem, j^lumbo nam graviora magis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1643>	" Ferrea crura mihi, latus est quasi lamina ferri,'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1644>	" Non est in toto corpore vena meo.'^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1645>	" iEnea ceu '^ pelvis cutis est mea, qu?e tamen ictus
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1646>	" Excipit '^ incassura, nam ^^ nihil inde dolet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1647>	" Non ego verberibus, non^*^ per maledieta, perire
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1648>	" Possum, malleolis vix puto posse mori.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1649>	" Cur mea me mater maledicto ^ fudit ab alvo ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1650>	" Cur g-ladio jugulum non dedit ipsa meum?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1651>	" Tristis abortivum si me peperisset, in tevum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1652>	" Quam fortunata quamque beata foret!
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1653>	" Cur lupuH esuriens partes non venit in illas,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1654>	" Tolleret et^ partum dum tener esset adhuc ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1655>	" Cur mea me mater primis devovit in annis,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1656>	" Atqne venire citum '' sfepe rogavit eum ?
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1657>	" Huic ego* pro certo non solum praeda futurus,^
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1658>	" Esca sed et rapidis auguror esse Jupis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1659>	" Nam eeler eventus, si fas est credere farajo,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1660>	" Maternis precibus sernper adesse solet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1661>	Somnium Burnelli.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1662>	" Quoque magis moveor, me certa pericula terrent,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1663>	" Praeterita nocte somnia visa mihi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1664>	" Nam pater et mater Domino pro me prece fusa
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1665>	" Orabant, et in htec verba fuere preces.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1666>	' Esto, Deus, nobis elemens,^ et ab ore luporum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1667>	" ' Eripe BurneHum, facque redire domum.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1668>	' Sanus et incokimis patrias peregrinus ad oras
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1669>	" ' Burnellus redeat, liber ab ore lupi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1670>	' Non leo, non ' pardus, nee peste nocentior omni
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1671>	" ' Rusticus obsistat vel dominetur ei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1672>	' Transeat immunis per compita quseque viarum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1673>	" ' Olfaetu careat bestia qu?eque suo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1674>	" ' Sit canis elinguis, catulo non pareat * auris ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1675>	" ' Currere ne possit sit mala gutta lupo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1676>	' ' Quern quia nos'-^ aliis plus formidamus, ab ipso
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1677>	" ' Protege Burnellum, facque redire domum.'
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1678>	Unde '*? per antiphrasim quia somnia ssepe resolvi
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1679>	" Consuevere, magis mens mea visa timet.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1680>	" Qualia cevnnntur nocturno soiiinia visu,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1681>	" Talia non debent inane secjuente sequi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1682>	" Sed vice eouversa sunt expoueuda vicissim,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1683>	" Atque per antiphrasiin somnia, crede mihi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1684>	" Si bona vidisti,^ tunc aspera multa sequentur ;
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1685>	" Si mala, non dubites prospera multa sequi.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1686>	" Sic mea consuevit exponere somnia mater,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1687>	" Sicut erat prudens atque diserta nimis.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1688>	" Mater ob banc causam litem cum patre frequenter
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1689>	" Instituit, super bis plurima verba sei-ens.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1690>	" Ipse tamen matri semper contraria sensit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1691>	" Et sua dicebat dogmata falsa fore.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1692>	" Utpote qui fuerat astronmi lege peritus,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1693>	" A puero doctus signa notare poll.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1694>	Sententla BurneUi dc [sf] faciendo episcopor
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1695>	" Sed quodcunque '^ mei super bis sensere parentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1696>	" Mens mea tota tremit, plena timore novo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1697>	" Cur tamen boc timeam ? cum non sint' jure " tiinenda
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1698>	" Qua3 nequeuut alio stave vcl ire niodo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1699>	" Fata, nee id dubito, quicquid statuere'' futurum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1700>	" Eveniet ; contra nemo venire potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1701>	" Rebus in liumanis seu decrevere futurum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1702>	" Fata, quod ^ eveniat semper oportet ita.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1703>	" Nemo sui fati vel devitare tenorem
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1704>	" Vel mutare^ potest; ergo uec ipse mei.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1705>	" Et tamen ignoro quse sunt mea fata futura,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1706>	" Prospera vel dura, seu mala sive bona.**
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1707>	" Pontificem forsan me constituere futurum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 1708>	" Inque mea patria sedis bonore frui.
