<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2359>	" Pinguia concedens, qutE sunt affinia carni,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2360>	" Sic tamen ut nunquam sit raanifesta caro.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2361>	" Bellum cum carne, pacem cum pinguibus esse,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2362>	" Pacis amatores hoc statuere modo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2363>	" Carnis honestatem sic conservare volentes,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2364>	" Ne contra carnem lex inhonesta foret.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2365>	" Si foi'et exclusa penitus caro, carnis honestas
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2366>	" Lresam se posset de ratione queri.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2367>	" Si foret in totuni sine conditione recepta,'*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2368>	" Ssepe daret causam materiamque mali.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2369>	" Unde nee admissa penitus, nee tota repulsa,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2370>	" Exulat, in patria menstrua facta sua.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2371>	De Canonic'is secularikas.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2372>	" Sunt et canonici qui secularesque vocati*
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2373>	" Nomen ab officio jiromeruere suo.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2374>	" His quodcunque libet, nova lex, licitumque ^ sub isto
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2375>	" Canone constituit vivere tota cohors.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2376>	" Hi nihil excipiunt, nee dicunt despiciendum,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2377>	" Quicquid in obsequio corporis esse *" potest.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2378>	" lUud prfficipue tamen instituere, tenendum
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2379>	" Omnibus in tota posteritate sua
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2380>	" Lex vetus ut suasit, ne quilibet absque sua sit,
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2381>	" Et quod quisque suas possit habere duas.
<nigel_wireker. specstult. 2382>	" Hi sunt ([ui luundmn cam llore eadcnte tenentco,
